      "title": "After Work, We’ll Have Each Other",
      "gist": "A world without work would be relational, and such worlds turn out small and exclusionary, so work's impersonal dignity is worth keeping.",
      "question": "Relational society — why might a world where relationships replace work leave us worse off? (case studies)"
    },
